NAME
       wget - download files from web servers

SYNOPSIS
       wget [-O FILE] [-P DIRECTORY] [-q] [-c] [-N] URL...

DESCRIPTION
       wget downloads each URL (http, https or ftp) and saves it in the
       current directory under the name at the end of the URL, showing
       progress. It is in the wget package, which is not always installed;
       curl -O does the same job and is always there.

OPTIONS
       -O, --output-document=FILE
              Save to FILE. -O - writes the download to standard output.

       -P, --directory-prefix=DIR
              Save into DIR.

       -q, --quiet
              Print nothing.

       -nv, --no-verbose
              Print only one line per file.

       -c, --continue
              Resume a download that was interrupted.

       -N, --timestamping
              Download only when the server's copy is newer.

       --tries=N
              Try N times.

       --no-check-certificate
              Do not check the server's TLS certificate (test servers only).

EXAMPLES
       Download a file into /root:

           wget -P /root http://utility.lab.example.com/files/users.txt

       Save a page under another name:

           wget -O /var/www/html/index.html http://utility.lab.example.com/files/index.html

SEE ALSO
       curl(1)
